WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.378
Meet Memoket Note, an agent-native writing workspace.

00:00:03.458 --> 00:00:07.666
This personal open-source project is built on the memoket-kite memory engine.

00:00:07.746 --> 00:00:12.847
It brings AI writing actions, source-backed memory and reviewable edits into the same note.

00:00:12.927 --> 00:00:16.298
A writing agent harness coordinates the work behind the scenes.

00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:21.513
A writing task starts with a note, its purpose and the material you want to use.

00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:28.484
The editor keeps this state together, so you can work on the draft while the agent retrieves context and proposes changes.

00:00:28.564 --> 00:00:31.199
You remain responsible for the final text.

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:34.937
For a small task, use a direct writing action.

00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:38.289
Select a paragraph to rewrite, polish or verify.

00:00:38.369 --> 00:00:41.221
Continue at the cursor when you need the next passage.

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:45.942
For a longer task, start a workflow with the note goal and completion criteria.

00:00:46.022 --> 00:00:48.511
Each entry point carries the relevant scope.

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:51.600
Memoket-kite supplies long-term memory.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.338
Note uses its facts and source links to bring relevant evidence into the writing task.

00:00:56.418 --> 00:01:00.829
You can inspect recalled material, collect it in the tray and cite it in the draft.

00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:05.672
Retrieval is evidence to review, not a guarantee that a generated claim is correct.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:11.798
The writing agent harness manages task state and tools, and turns a writing request into a loop.

00:01:11.878 --> 00:01:15.323
First it prepares material, then drafts or revises.

00:01:15.403 --> 00:01:20.675
Deterministic checks inspect constraints such as citations, output shape and repetition.

00:01:20.755 --> 00:01:23.998
A model judge assesses the configured writing dimensions.

00:01:24.078 --> 00:01:28.869
The policy uses that feedback to choose another round, repair, pause or stop.

00:01:29.542 --> 00:01:31.021
Changes stay reviewable.

00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:34.379
Inspect individual edits and decide what to keep or revert.

00:01:34.459 --> 00:01:37.272
Run snapshots and note history support recovery.

00:01:37.352 --> 00:01:42.653
The harness has explicit limits and stopping conditions, and can retain an earlier best round.

00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:47.248
Automated checks help you review the result, but they do not replace your judgment.

00:01:47.917 --> 00:01:52.987
For example, start a weekly report by setting the audience and what the report must cover.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:58.155
Gather notes and other material, then let the harness prepare evidence, draft and check.

00:01:58.235 --> 00:02:03.985
Review the proposed changes and verify their citations before exporting or sharing the finished report.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:10.622
Memoket Note is a personal project, with application code licensed under AGPL version three.

00:02:10.702 --> 00:02:14.355
The separate memoket-kite engine uses the Apache two license.

00:02:14.435 --> 00:02:17.472
Configure your own model and transcription services.

00:02:17.552 --> 00:02:24.709
This is a conceptual walkthrough of the implemented architecture, rather than a live product demonstration or performance benchmark.
